    "title": "Douglas County Residents Invited to Join Committees on Proposed Emergency Communications Tax - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 hours ago The Douglas County Board of Commissioners is seeking residents to serve on Pro and Con committees for a proposed 0.1% sales and use tax increase. The tax would fund local emergency communications systems and facilities. On September 30, 2025, the Board approved a resolution to put this measure on the ballot. The goal is to provide ongoing funding for emergency communications infrastructure.\nEach committee, one in favor and one against the measure, can have up to three members. All members must live in Douglas County. Interested residents should submit an application with contact information and a brief statement of interest. The deadline is 5:00 p.m. on Tuesday, November 25, 2025. Applications should be emailed to Doug Jones, RiverCom Executive Director. More information is available in the Douglas County Elections Guide and on the County Auditor's website.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
